From ccd6a120ded11fc3e875cada756d24ff17b809a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Comet0322 <maint@sim.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): load fonts from @fontsource-variable instead of
 next/font/google

next/font/google downloads the faces from the Google Fonts CDN during
`next build`, so the web image cannot be built on a network without
internet access. Load the same fontsource packages and files the desktop
renderer already uses; globals.css maps the families onto the existing
--font-inter / --font-geist-mono / --font-jetbrains-mono /
--font-source-serif variables, so every stack built on them is unchanged.

The geist-mono, jetbrains-mono and source-serif-4 versions move into the
pnpm catalog so web and desktop stay on the same files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
